# MASTER BUILD PROMPT — REQUIEM: THE GHOST ARCHIVE

Build a complete, premium, cinematic, full-stack web application named **REQUIEM — The Ghost Archive** from scratch.

Do not build a generic SaaS dashboard, a basic chatbot, or a static landing page. Create an immersive, highly scrollable, fantasy-inspired digital archaeology experience with the visual quality of a premium fantasy game website.

Use the supplied reference image as the primary VISUAL DIRECTION: dramatic full-screen character artwork, dark purple storm atmosphere, glowing magical energy, elegant metallic typography, deep shadows, atmospheric lighting, cinematic composition, and navigation that blends into the artwork.

IMPORTANT: The fantasy character in the reference is only a visual style reference. REQUIEM must have its own original identity, artwork, symbols, and visual assets. Do not copy another game's logo, character, artwork, or trademark.

The application must combine this cinematic visual identity with a genuinely useful open-weight AI project investigation tool.

==================================================
1. PRODUCT IDENTITY AND PURPOSE
==================================================

Product name: REQUIEM
Full name: REQUIEM — The Ghost Archive
Tagline: "Every abandoned project leaves a ghost."
Supporting line: "Recover the intent. Trace the unfinished. Give forgotten code another life."

Core purpose:
REQUIEM investigates abandoned or unfinished software projects. It examines supplied README files, source files, documentation, and actual Git history when available. It reconstructs the project's likely purpose, identifies unfinished features, connects findings to source evidence, and creates a practical revival roadmap.

The central metaphor is that forgotten code is an archaeological site and AI is the investigator uncovering the story left behind.

Target users:
- Open-source contributors
- Developers investigating old repositories
- Students learning software architecture
- Maintainers reviving abandoned projects
- Hackathon participants

This project is being built for the Hacktoberfest "Ghost in the Machine" challenge.

Its use of an actual open-weight model must be a core technical feature, not a decorative claim.

